# ---- Entries below were written retroactively at the end of the work session that built the castle campaign
# ---- (AGENTS.md was added to the repo partway through, so these were not logged one by one).

[2026-11-17] chore: dependencies, lint config and .gitignore
  files: pyproject.toml, uv.lock, .gitignore
  why:   the game needs pygame (it was not declared; pip was the only dependency). Added pytest and ruff as a dev group and a ruff config (E9 + F rules).
  notes: `uv sync` installed pytest and ruff into .venv and removed pip from it. .gitignore ignores .venv, .idea, caches, rogue_settings.json, qa/shots.

[2026-11-17] refactor: split main.py into the game/ package (no behaviour change)
  files: main.py, game/ (config, gfx, classes, sprites, levels, inputs, loot, player, enemies, arena, app)
  why:   main.py was 1,533 lines and the work ahead would have doubled it. Needed testable modules and a clean controller seam.
  notes: done with a script that sliced the original by line range. Verified with a deterministic bot simulation of all 6 old areas that matched
         the original exactly (kept as tests/test_baseline.py in commit 55bb2a5). Display creation moved out of import time so tests run headless.

[2026-11-17] feat: data-driven levels, six castle levels and compounding difficulty
  files: game/levels.py, game/config.py, game/arena.py
  why:   brief: 6 levels (basement, jungle, holy cathedral, necropolis, mafia penthouse, observatory roof) and +25% enemy damage / -25% damage taken per level.
  notes: difficulty() = (0.75**level, 1.25**level), constants DMG_TAKEN_STEP / DMG_DEAL_STEP in config.py. Damage floor of 1. Level 1 shows control hints.
         Replaced AREAS (6 old themed areas) with LEVELS; old Sunken Ruin, Ember Caverns and Frost Keep backgrounds were dropped.

[2026-11-17] feat: new enemies (zombie, wolf, bunny/wolf/cat beast men, holy knight, lich, mafia gunman, alien, drone) and enemy projectiles/hazards
  files: game/enemies.py, game/sprites_extra.py, game/sprites.py, game/arena.py, game/player.py
  why:   brief item 2. Enemy AI is now driven by ESTATS keys (hop, lunge, fly, ranged, summon, shield, dodge, climb). Perfect block reflects bullets.
  notes: Player.take now accepts sx=None (unblockable) and src=None. "Elon Musk" is the final boss's display name via config.ALIEN_NAME.

[2026-11-17] feat: six bosses, boss flow and boss HP bar
  files: game/bosses.py, game/arena.py, game/cutscenes.py
  why:   brief item 3. Flow is waves -> boss -> portal. Patterns telegraph, unlock by phase (66% / 33%), bosses resist stun and knockback.
  notes: BOSS_HP is a tunable list. Boss damage numbers were tuned down after the balance report (beastlord 18->13, don 12->9, tycoon 15->12, fewer bullets/rockets).

[2026-11-17] feat: holy chest on level 3 with class weapons and curses; gear persists across levels
  files: game/loot.py, game/player.py (apply_gear), game/arena.py, game/app.py
  why:   brief: boss drops a chest, 75% class holy weapon / 25% stronger cursed weapon, player chooses whether to take it.
  notes: holy +25% ATK; cursed +70% ATK plus one curse (take +30-35% damage, or max HP -20/-25%, or cooldowns +40%). The chest is placed beside the boss corpse.

[2026-11-17] feat: cutscenes (level intro card, castle-climb after each boss, ending)
  files: game/cutscenes.py, game/app.py
  why:   brief item 5. All are procedural, skippable with Tab / Esc / slash.

[2026-11-17] feat: skip-tutorial button
  files: game/arena.py, game/app.py, game/inputs.py
  why:   brief item 1. Tab or a mouse click on the on-screen button. Marks tutorial_done and saves it. Motion gained skip_p (Tab) so a controller button can use it later.

[2026-11-17] feat: developer mode, command-line flags and headless selftest
  files: game/devmode.py, game/app.py, game/selftest.py, main.py
  why:   brief item 4. --dev / ROGUE_DEV=1 / --level N / --gallery / --selftest. Dev keys: 1-6 [ ] N B X G V T Y C H F1. Never saved to settings.

[2026-11-17] feat: make_motions() factory and controller plan
  files: game/inputs.py, docs/controller-protocol.md
  why:   later stage: Elegoo UNO + GY-521. Only the seam and a written plan exist; no controller code. The sketch in the doc is untested on hardware.

[2026-11-17] test: pytest suite (~160 tests), bots, selftest, balance report, screenshots, QA agent
  files: tests/*, game/qabot.py, qa/ (run_qa.py, balance.py, render_shots.py, render_sprites.py, CHECKLIST.md), .claude/agents/qa.md
  why:   user asked for a QA that checks code quality and outcomes.
  notes: deleted tests/test_baseline.py and tests/golden_baseline.json on purpose. They compared the new game against the ORIGINAL 6 areas, which no longer exist
         (AGENTS.md says a baseline may change only for an intended gameplay change: this was one). The refactor was verified against it before deletion (see the refactor entry).

[2026-11-17] fix: bugs from v4 found by the new tests
  files: game/gfx.py, game/arena.py, game/config.py, game/player.py
  why:   (1) blit_ent crashed with "invalid color argument" for negative tints, so drawing any looted corpse crashed the game (existed in v4).
         (2) enemies were drawn facing away from the player (flip condition inverted in v4). (3) a player standing at the exit when an area cleared left the level
         instantly: added PORTAL_GRACE = 1.5 s. (4) load_settings lost tutorial_done when the file had no "keys". (5) damage could round to 0.
  notes: each has a regression test.

[2026-11-17] docs: README.md brought up to date
  files: README.md
  why:   the earlier README described a mid-change working tree. Now describes the finished behaviour, dev mode, tests, QA, and replaces the stale Known issues.

